  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Asia Pacific Regional Governance UK-Based Programme-funded Role</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This budget component covers UK-based programme staff whose primary function is to design, manage, and deliver the Asia-Pacific Regional Governance Programme, which is ODA-funded. The staffs provide technical oversight, strategic guidance, programme management, and quality assurance for activities that directly support governance, institutional strengthening, and development outcomes in ODA-eligible countries in South East Asia and the Pacific. These functions directly contribute to the economic development and welfare of countries on the OECD DAC List of ODA-Eligible Countries. As permitted under OECD DAC rules, the cost of administering and managing ODA programmes&#x2014;when the work is directly attributable to designing, delivering, or overseeing development activities&#x2014;can be counted as ODA. The work undertaken by these UK-based staff directly enables the programme&#x2019;s governance reforms, capacity-building initiatives, and policy support in partner countries, and therefore qualifies as ODA-eligible administrative and programme management expenditure.</narrative>
  </description>
